From: tb710fu-arch-linux
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: TB710FU battery current sign

The TB710FU ADSP firmware reports the battery current positive while discharging
(+1 A idle) and negative while charging (-9 A on 45 W PD). The power_supply ABI
wants negative for discharging, so upower showed a charging tablet as discharging.
Flip it for this board only.
---
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1543,6 +1543,10 @@
 			break;
 		case BATT_CURR_NOW:
 			battmgr->status.current_now = le32_to_cpu(resp->intval.value);
+			/* TB710FU ADSP firmware: positive while discharging; the power_supply
+			 * ABI (and upower) want negative, or charging shows as discharging */
+			if (of_machine_is_compatible("lenovo,tb710fu"))
+				battmgr->status.current_now = -battmgr->status.current_now;
 			break;
 		case BATT_TEMP:
 			val = le32_to_cpu(resp->intval.value);
